# Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) Security Policy

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates the creation of a Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) security policy designed to protect organizational data when employees use personal devices to access company resources.

## Purpose
The purpose of this policy is to define security requirements for personal devices used for work, including authentication, encryption, VPN use, data segregation, and compliance expectations.

## Skills Demonstrated
- Security policy development
- Risk mitigation
- Cybersecurity documentation
- Governance and compliance awareness
- Professional written communication

## Policy Topics Covered
- Introduction and purpose
- Scope
- Security controls
- VPN requirements
- Data segregation
- Privacy statement
- Consequences for violations
- Communication plan

## Framework Alignment
This project was developed with reference to cybersecurity best practices such as:
- NIST guidance for mobile device security
- SANS security principles

